      "reconciliation_finding": "The 85.71-hour passive vaccine holdover (3.60 kWh_th / 0.042 kWh_th/hr) holds ONLY at nominal 32 C ambient with fresh PCM. At 43 C WHO PQS extreme ambient temperature, heat ingress rises by 1.407x (to 0.0591 kWh_th/hr), reducing passive zero-sun holdover to 60.90 hours (and 51.77 hours after 15% cyclic PCM degradation). During the 72-hour storm at 18% daytime irradiance, OpenLine SDD-PCM still achieves 0 excursion hours because Priority-2 daytime solar compressor top-ups replenish ~1.5 kWh_th/day; however, in a 120-hour near-zero-irradiance (4%) typhoon blackout (Scenario D), SDD-PCM suffers 38 hours of vaccine excursion (>8 C) once the 85.71-hour passive holdover expires, whereas Priority-Controlled LiFePO4 suffers 14 hours and the Competent Hybrid (1.5 kWh LiFePO4 + PCM) reduces excursion to 8 hours."
    },
    "nuanced_comparative_conclusion": "1. Fair Priority-Control Falsification Result: Adding OpenLine's priority controller and 1,500 L water header tank to the conventional 4 kWh LiFePO4 battery system (`CONV_PRIORITY_CONTROLLED_LI_BATTERY`) completely eliminates its 72-hour monsoon vaccine excursion (0h vs 5h unprioritized at 32C, and 0h vs 28h unprioritized at 43C) and restores 100.0% water reliability. This proves that the 72-hour monsoon vaccine failure in Civilization Frontier 001 was driven by missing priority load-shedding and undersized water storage, NOT by lithium battery chemistry inability to survive a 72-hour storm.\n2. Where OpenLine SDD-PCM (`OPENLINE_SDD_PCM_PRIORITY_ROUTER`) Genuinely Wins Against Fair Priority-Controlled LiFePO4: (a) 10-Year Total Cost: $4,095 vs $8,465 at 32C (-51.6%, saving $4,370) and $4,095 vs $10,265 at 43C (-60.1%, saving $6,170); (b) Chemical Battery E-Waste: 0.0 kg vs 135.0-180.0 kg over 10 years; (c) BMS Single-Point-of-Failure Immunity (Scenario E): 0h vaccine excursion vs 18h excursion when the battery BMS trips; (d) Crop Spoilage Parity/Edge: 12.37% vs 12.52% at 32C (19.60% vs 21.21% in Year-8 aged equipment).\n3. Where Pure SDD-PCM Loses to Priority-Controlled LiFePO4 & Hybrid (`COMPETENT_HYBRID_SMALL_LFP_PLUS_PCM`, $6,045 10-yr cost): In a 120-hour (5-day) near-zero-sun typhoon blackout (Scenario D, 4% irradiance), pure SDD-PCM suffers 38 hours of vaccine excursion once its 85.7-hour passive ice-bank is exhausted (because daytime solar is too weak to overcome compressor start thresholds), whereas Priority-Controlled LiFePO4 suffers 14 hours and the Competent Hybrid (1.5 kWh LiFePO4 + PCM) suffers only 8 hours (and achieves the lowest crop spoilage across Scenarios A [9.79%] and C [16.67%]).",
